I had an incredible game going.

Started a werewolf undead slayer, Daniel Osbourne, on
antisymmetric.com.

In the first room, there is a tool.  Surprise, it's not a chest, but a
lamp. I try to bless it, and find it's already blessed. A few rubs and
by turn 12 I'm wearing a ring of polymorph control.

Shops are common in the early levels, all offering identify service.
There is also a full weapon-works shop, a tool shop and a WAND shop
that both offer charging.
The mine town altar is cross-aligned, and no altars in the main
dungeon until level 15 or so.
I don't find a potion of gain level, so I solve sokoban for the bag
instead of upgrading my oilskin sack.
Eventually, I find a handy amulet of ESP.

Opera cloaks are protection, not magic resist, so I never end up
getting MR.
On level 22 there is a dragon room where the first silver dragon is
kind enough to drop scales. No magic boots, gloves, or helms show up. 
I suppose I should have polypiled for them, but I had not identified
"restore ability".

Without MR, Vecna's level is too risky, even though I've got a wand of
fire to burn Elbereth.  There is a major scare when a Vampire mage
summons a minotaur, but I eventually take it out with my pistol.

Nightmare's level is also too scary, since I've never faced it before.

The only artifacts that I'm given from saccing are Grimtooth and
Deathsword. Very unimpressive.

Eventually, I fought a cockatrice.  With my MC of 3, I knew that the
odds of a successful stoning attack were about 1%. Of course - you are
slowing down.

Do I turn to stone? ... No.
I bite my lizard corpse - Do I choke? ... No.
Hmmm.  But I've lost my intrinsic speed.  Better fix that.

